						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Having a level 62 druid main I look at the druid re-envisionment and think of possiblities. The way my guild is currently our only clerics are bots or low level alts, so in many cases when in a group I play the role of main healer. This I don&#039;t mind, and never have since I&#039;m not manic about being a DPS druid. <br /><br />The Defensive stance would help me in groups because it would give me the opportunity to toss in a couple of DoT&#039;s here and there for just a little extra speed on the kills, but put a nice boost on the druids CH equivalent. More chance of rescuing a tank if he goes down faster than I can mange if I&#039;ve got an extra 25% on that or any of my other heals. Along with the AA&#039;s like Healing Adept and Healing Gift, which I don&#039;t yet have, it would prove to be a nice boost to any group that couldn&#039;t find a cleric.<br /><br />Were I to take the Offensive stance I would be able to take on possibly more challenging mobs were I solo quad kiting, or root DoTing. If I got into a bind where my hit points were going down faster than they ought to be I could throw out an Egress and be out without more than a little sweat, and not worry about healing anyone, but myself until in safe quarters. And I&#039;m a druid... if I&#039;ve got uber hit points and need a big heal when I&#039;m soloing I&#039;ve got the wrong gear on or I&#039;m not doing something right.<br /><br />Edit: I r teh Typo Quean</td>
